y doing with local  authorities  um I'm very committed to  improving the engagement we have with  local authorities particularly those in  rural areas but um let me just not leap  to a particular solution but I will look  at what things we can do going forward  certainly not closing my mind to that  solution  thank you Chris Secretary State just a  few closing questions  um on buses what is the department doing  I know this is before your time so you  might want to write to us what is the  department doing with the bus service  network reviews that local transport  authorities were required to submit by  July  one of the things we haven't touched on  today  um is Road haulage and drivers driver  facilities and the planning regime  that's in place currently that negates  improving the lot for Road all his  drivers would you like to give us an  update on that rather than answer  something now as well as on your  thoughts on the supply chain and any  issues that have been apparent over the  past two three years and moving forward  over the next two I'll we'll write you  with a fuller answer but you you may be  aware of of what um Richard Holden the  rose Minister set out last week and set  out some  um support that we've made available to  improve the facilities for hdv drivers  which I think is really important and  we've obviously done a lot of work with  the industry on on making sure we can  make more tests available so that  actually we can increase the number of  HD hdv drivers to deal with the shortage  we saw we've made good progress on that  it's not it's not done yet but we've  made good progress and that maybe we'll  give some more information about that  when we write to the committee I don't  know whether Bernadette wants to add  anything now um just to say that I think  actually we've made good progress as  you'll recall last year  um uh we had a sort of 33 Point action  plan I think to deal with a then quiet  pressing issue of HEB driver shortages  of which  um uh the testing was a key part I think  we have made good progress I think the  industry is now reporting a much  improved situation in terms of  availability of hgv drivers so I think  we're feeling uh more confident about  that I think your questions may also  refer to our future plans for Freight  Beyond it specifically Drive facilities  I know the government has made some  monies available which has been welcome  indeed but I can see the planning regime  is the real is the real roadblock okay  so it's a planning machine  okay and  Bernadette dvla yes  um are there any any things you'd like  any Salient points you'd like to make  the committee aware of have there been  any further improvements I think as you  now  the dvla have now addressed all of the  backlogs the one remaining area of  difficulty is drivers Medicals which is  an important area I and the CEO and my  director General responsible for this  area gave evidence to the Public  Accounts committee a couple of weeks ago  on this and I'm I refer you to that I  think it's an exhaustive session with  many questions  um and I think a lot of progress has  been made as that as I hope our  testimony  um demonstrated I do think what it also  what we also  um acknowledged is that there are still  significant challenges around drivers  medical partly that's dealing with the  backlog but I think there is  um a prospect we do expect that to have  been addressed by the beginning of the  new year but I think uh what the  committee uh identified correctly was as  a sort of wider systemic issue it this  is a really challenging area of the  dvla's work partly because of the nature  of an aging population with multiple  medical conditions who naturally want to  continue to drive live but we need to  find a system capable of dealing with  those cases I think in a more effective  way and that is certainly something that  I and my colleagues in dvla are looking  very hard at but I think on the whole  um I believe tha